<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="38e42eae-4666-59b4-bee8-15c5f4999f78" activityNameId="0e496f2e-b3fe-55e8-a783-273a88629dc0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Petrol, burned in building machine, with particle filter</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Petrol, burned in building machine, with particle filter
The consumption of lubricating oil are taken from ecoinvent v2.2, as well as emission patern during the combustion. Values for CO2, CO, NOx, CH4 and NMHC were taken from the Non-road database and represent average factors for gasoline-powered, four-stroke, hand-guided tamping rammers and vibratory plates. 
UUID: ce890b07-c419-41bf-83b9-ff19734f38f6
This dataset is based on the process "Diesel, burned in building machine {GLO}|". Compared to this reference process, the dataset includes only lubricating oil, diesel fuel and the emissions produced during the combustion of 1 MJ of petrol fuel in an average building machine in Switzerland. 
Location: Europe
Technology: The process "petrol, burned in building machine, with particle filter/MJ/CH" has been modified to generate a dataset that consider the emissions produced during the combustion of 1 MJ of petrol fuel in a building machine in Switzerland.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Statistics
Extrapolations: Emissions taken from "Diesel, burned in building machine {GLO}"
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ce890b07-c419-41bf-83b9-ff19734f38f6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
